-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Altered Beast
  Publisher   Activision, 1988
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Altered Beast (1988)(Activision)[128K].z80
  MD5         9df49e056fdf38a2f6da21fc4dfbf34f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Figures in the arcade's colours: the centurion with skin, blond
              hair, a red loincloth and brown sandals, zombies in purple robes
              with grey heads, fiery transformation clouds, pale wolves.
              Player two and a wolf's hit flash keep the game's colours. Only
              sprite colours change. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Changes     1.1: Enhanced colours, after the arcade, as a menu choice.

  Note        Keys: SPACE starts; 6 left, 7 right, 8 duck, 9 jump, 0 punch;
              ENTER on the menu adds a second player. Every figure, graves and
              the boss included, is hardware sprites, so the centurions and
              the beasts no longer take the colours of the scenery they cross;
              the scenery, the panel and the titles stay as the game draws
              them. Also fixes a crash on the Next: the game's interrupt
              handlers ran twice a frame there. The first level only, as in
              this file: the later levels load from tape, and game over and
              the level's end wait for that tape as the original does.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite credits
   2  Infinite lives
   3  Infinite energy

  From an archive .pok, its level-1 lines, each checked against the code (the
  DEC of the credits, lives and energy counts); infinite lives and energy were
  also on in a recording of the whole level. The other levels' lines are for
  code this file does not hold.

